course: dictionary
lesson: 5921
title: Many meanings of marriage
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning, and the sentence tells you which meaning to use. Read the clues around the word. «Dad's mother is Mum's mother-in-law, a relative by marriage.» Here marriage means the legal link between two people who are husband and wife, which joins whole families together.
explain: «In history, royal marriages joined powerful families.» Here marriages means weddings, the ceremonies where two people get married. Test your meaning in the sentence: "royal weddings joined powerful families" still makes sense, so you have chosen well.
explain: Marriage can also mean the time two people are married, as in «a long, happy marriage». Ask yourself what the word is describing. If it describes how long something lasted or how it felt, the time meaning is likely.
fact: Marriage is a noun: a marriage, marriages.
fact: Marriage can mean the legal relationship between two people who are husband and wife, or partners.
fact: A marriage can also be a wedding, the ceremony where two people get married.
fact: Marriage can mean the time two people are married, as in «a long, happy marriage».
fact: Useful phrases include get married, a happy marriage and marriage proposal.
exercise: «Dad's mother is Mum's mother-in-law, a relative by marriage.» What is a relative by marriage? | A cousin who lives far away | *A family member joined by the law of marriage | A pet that belongs to the family | A friend who came to the wedding
exercise: «In history, royal marriages joined powerful families.» What does marriages mean here? | Pieces of jewellery | Holidays by the sea | Long journeys across the country | *Weddings, the ceremonies where two people get married
exercise: Ella says, «Their marriage has lasted fifty years.» What does marriage mean here? | A law about money | *The time two people have been married | An argument between two families | A wedding dress
test: The marriage took place in a small church in June. What does marriage mean in this sentence? | The legal link between two families | A holiday by the sea | *A wedding ceremony | A long, happy time together
test: They plan to get married next spring. What does get married mean? | To go on a holiday abroad | To move house to a new town | *To become husband and wife in a wedding | To have a birthday party
exam: «Sam's grandad said his marriage of forty years was the best thing in his life.» What does marriage mean here? | A wedding invitation | A holiday trip | A law about families | *The time he has been married
